{"schema_version":"v1","refusal":{"is_refusal":false,"reason":null,"safe_alternative":null},"assumptions":["Use standard complex/real Fourier series for a 2\\pi-periodic square wave with odd sine-only expansion; sample grid of 2000 points for plots.","Measure Gibbs overshoot as maximum pointwise error in a fixed small neighborhood around each discontinuity (e.g., radius 0.05)."],"problem":{"original_text":"Let f(x) be the 2\\pi-periodic extension of the square wave f(x)=1 for x in (0,\\pi), f(x)=-1 for x in (-\\pi,0). Let S_N(x) be the N-term Fourier partial sum. Tasks: (a) For N in {5,15,50,200}, plot f(x) and S_N(x) over [-\\pi,\\pi] on same axes; measure overshoot and describe Gibbs. (b) For same N plot pointwise error |S_N-f| and zoom near x=0 showing shrinking region vs persistent height. (c) Plot |\\hat f(n)| vs n on log-log axes and fit slope relating to discontinuity. (d) Plot L^2 and L^\\infty-away-from-discontinuities errors vs N and explain rates. (e) Optional: compare Fej\\'er sums \\sigma_N with S_N.","normalized_text":"Square wave 2\\pi-periodic: f(x)=1 on (0,\\pi), f(x)=-1 on (-\\pi,0). Compute and analyze Fourier partial sums S_N for N in {5,15,50,200}: overlay plots with f, pointwise error and zoom, coefficient decay log-log, L^2 and uniform-away errors vs N, and optional Fej\\'er comparison.","detected_tasks":["fourier_series","convergence","spectral_decay","visualization","functions"]},"classification":{"grade_band":"undergraduate_lower","domain":"fourier_series","topic":"Fourier series and Gibbs phenomenon","difficulty":"medium"},"steps":[{"index":1,"title":"Define f and its Fourier coefficients","explanation":"Write the 2\\pi-periodic square wave and recall its sine-only Fourier expansion coefficients because f is odd. Use coefficient formula and closed form for sine coefficients.","math_latex":["f(x)=\\begin{cases}1&x\\in(0,\\pi)\\\\-1&x\\in(-\\pi,0)\\end{cases}","\\hat f(n)=\\frac{1}{\\pi}\\int_{-\\pi}^{\\pi}f(x)\\sin(nx)\\,dx=\\begin{cases}\\tfrac{4}{n\\pi}&n\\text{ odd}\\\\0&n\\text{ even}\\end{cases}"],"rules_used":["periodic_extension","Fourier_coefficient_formula","odd_function_simplification"]},{"index":2,"title":"Construct partial sums S_N","explanation":"Form S_N(x) as finite sum of sine modes using the nonzero odd coefficients. Use N to denote number of nonzero terms (odd-indexed modes up to the desired truncation).","math_latex":["S_N(x)=\\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}\\frac{4}{(2k+1)\\pi}\\sin((2k+1)x)"],"rules_used":["series_truncation","index_change"]},{"index":3,"title":"Set numerics and plotting grid","explanation":"Choose dense grid of M=2000 points on [-\\pi,\\pi] for plotting and evaluation. For each requested N compute S_N on that grid and the pointwise error. Save arrays to artifacts referenced below for backend plotting.","math_latex":["x_j=-\\pi+2\\pi\\frac{j}{M-1}\\quad j=0,\\dots,M-1","error_N(x)=|S_N(x)-f(x)|"],"rules_used":["uniform_sampling","discrete_evaluation"]},{"index":4,"title":"Produce overlay plots and measure overshoot","explanation":"For N in {5,15,50,200} produce overlay plots of f and S_N on [-\\pi,\\pi]. Measure overshoot near each discontinuity by finding the local maximum of S_N(x) in a small neighborhood and report overshoot height minus the jump limit value. Store plot data in artifacts.","math_latex":["overshoot_N=\\max_{|x-0|<\\delta}S_N(x)-1\\quad(\\text{choose }\\delta=0.05)","similar at x=\\pm\\pi"],"rules_used":["local_max_detection","neighborhood_measurement"]},{"index":5,"title":"Plot pointwise error and zoom near discontinuity","explanation":"Plot error_N on full interval and then produce a zoomed plot near x=0 (e.g., x\\in[-0.2,0.2]) to show the error peak width shrinking while peak height remains O(0.089...). Record data for the backend to visualize.","math_latex":["zoom_interval=[-0.2,0.2]","width_N=\\text{full width at half maximum of error peak}"],"rules_used":["FWHM","zoom_visualization"]},{"index":6,"title":"Coefficient magnitude plot and slope fit","explanation":"Compute |\\hat f(n)| for n up to n_max=2000 (or appropriate), plot on log-log axes, and fit a linear slope to estimate decay rate. Relate slope approximately -1 to the jump discontinuity (coefficients O(1/n)).","math_latex":["|\\hat f(2k+1)|=\\frac{4}{(2k+1)\\pi}","fit: \\log|\\hat f(n)|\\approx C-\\alpha\\log n"],"rules_used":["log_log_fit","decay_regularity_relation"]},{"index":7,"title":"Compute convergence metrics","explanation":"For a sweep of N values (Nlist=[5,10,20,50,100,200,400]) compute L^2 error on grid and L^\\infty error away from small neighborhoods of discontinuities (exclude intervals of radius 0.05 around jumps). Store errors for plotting versus N and compute observed empirical rates.","math_latex":["\\|S_N-f\\|_{L^2}\\approx\\sqrt{\\frac{2\\pi}{M}\\sum_j (S_N(x_j)-f(x_j))^2}","\\|S_N-f\\|_{L^\\infty,away}=\\max_{x\\notin U_\\delta}|S_N(x)-f(x)|"],"rules_used":["discrete_norm_approximation","exclusion_regions"]},{"index":8,"title":"Optional: Fej\\'er sums comparison","explanation":"Compute Ces\\'aro-averaged partial sums \\sigma_N(x)=(1/N)\\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}S_k(x) for same N list. Produce overlay plots of \\sigma_N and S_N and compute overshoot metrics to compare uniform convergence improvement.","math_latex":["\\sigma_N(x)=\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}S_k(x)"],"rules_used":["Cesaro_averaging","smoothing_effect"]}],"final_answer":{"answer_text":"Computation pending backend execution. The planned outputs are: (i) overlay plots f and S_N for N=5,15,50,200 with measured overshoot values stored in artifacts 'overshoot:N=5', 'overshoot:N=15', 'overshoot:N=50', 'overshoot:N=200'; (ii) pointwise error plots and zoomed-in error plots near x=0 stored as 'error:n=5','error:n=15','error:n=50','error:n=200' and zoomed variants; (iii) log-log coefficient magnitude plot and fitted slope stored as 'spectrum_samples:n=2000' and 'spectrum_fit'; (iv) convergence curves ||S_N-f||_{L^2} and ||S_N-f||_{L^\\infty,away} versus N stored as 'errors_vs_N'. All numeric results (overshoot heights, fitted slope, error norms, solver statistics) will be written into the listed artifacts when the backend executes the experiment.","answer_latex":"f(x)=\\n\\begin{cases}1&x\\in(0,\\pi)\\\\-1&x\\in(-\\pi,0)\\end{cases};\\quad\\hat f(2k+1)=\\frac{4}{(2k+1)\\pi};\\quad S_N(x)=\\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}\\frac{4}{(2k+1)\\pi}\\sin((2k+1)x)","values":[],"units":null},"visuals":{"should_visualize":true,"decision_reason":"Plots are explicitly requested in multiple steps (overlay, error, zoom, spectrum, convergence).","plots":[{"title":"Overlay: f and S_N for N=5,15,50,200","x_min":-3.141592653589793,"x_max":3.141592653589793,"y_min":-1.5,"y_max":1.5,"plot_kind":"cartesian_2d","x_scale":"linear","y_scale":"linear","series":[{"kind":"grid2d_ref","label":"f(x) sampled","expr_latex":null,"points":[],"data_ref":"f_grid:M=2000","color":"black","line_width":1.5,"line_style":"solid","marker_style":"none"},{"kind":"grid2d_ref","label":"S_N:n=5","expr_latex":null,"points":[],"data_ref":"S_N:n=5","color":"red","line_width":1.2,"line_style":"solid","marker_style":"none"},{"kind":"grid2d_ref","label":"S_N:n=15","expr_latex":null,"points":[],"data_ref":"S_N:n=15","color":"orange","line_width":1.2,"line_style":"solid","marker_style":"none"},{"kind":"grid2d_ref","label":"S_N:n=50","expr_latex":null,"points":[],"data_ref":"S_N:n=50","color":"green","line_width":1.2,"line_style":"solid","marker_style":"none"},{"kind":"grid2d_ref","label":"S_N:n=200","expr_latex":null,"points":[],"data_ref":"S_N:n=200","color":"blue","line_width":1.2,"line_style":"solid","marker_style":"none"}],"key_points":[{"label":"discontinuity at 0","x":0,"y":0}],"alternative_visual":null},{"title":"Pointwise error |S_N-f| and zoom near x=0","x_min":-3.141592653589793,"x_max":3.141592653589793,"y_min":0.0,"y_max":0.5,"plot_kind":"cartesian_2d","x_scale":"linear","y_scale":"linear","series":[{"kind":"grid2d_ref","label":"error N=5","expr_latex":null,"points":[],"data_ref":"error:n=5","color":"red","line_w